{
  "title": "Web: decompose ViewRecipePage.tsx (1246-line god component) and \
converge its AI handlers with the Cookbook bulk path",
  "description": "ramekin-ui/src/pages/ViewRecipePage.tsx:69-635 holds ~30 \
signals and ~25 async handlers covering unrelated concerns: recipe load, \
delete modal, version compare/revert, AI enrich (+ custom enrich), photo \
generation, title normalization, description generation, rescrape polling, \
shopping-list modal, and meal-plan modal.\n\
\n\
Extract self-contained pieces into child components/hooks that own their own \
state: meal-plan modal (172-179/605-633), version compare (486-516), \
enrichment (339-483).\n\
\n\
Two related warts to fix while in there:\n\
\n\
1. Inconsistent error surfacing: some handlers use extractApiError (good: \
:419, :438) while siblings hardcode a generic string and discard the caught \
error — :479 (custom enrichment), :507 (compare), :532 (description, ignores \
err entirely), :575 (rescrape). Route all catches through extractApiError(err, \
fallback).\n\
\n\
2. The per-recipe handlers \
handleGeneratePhoto/handleNormalizeTitle/handleGenerateDescription (:410-536) \
are the N=1 form of CookbookPage's bulk handlers (see \
p3-web-cookbook-bulk-ops-dedupe) with divergent error handling — express them \
as the 1-item case of the shared helper once it exists.\n\
\n\
Web-only: this is component decomposition, no behavior change; iOS god-view \
has its own issue (p3-ios-recipe-detail-view-model).",
